#. Tag: member
#: conf-options-table.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option was added in &kdesrc-build; 1.16. Prior to 20.06 this option was "
"used to configure the fetch URL instead of the push URL. As of 20.06 "
"<literal>https</literal> is always used when updating KDE projects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:93
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Note that this option relies on information available from the &kde; "
#| "project database, so this feature only works for these modules. See also "
#| "<xref linkend=\"kde-projects-module-sets\"/>."
msgid ""
"This option only applies to modules from a <link linkend=\"kde-projects-"
"module-sets\">&kde; project</link> repository."
msgstr ""
"Esta opción depende de información dispoñíbel na base de datos to proxecto "
"&kde;, polo que esta funcionalidade unicamente ten efecto neses módulos. "
"Véxase tamén <xref linkend=\"kde-projects-module-sets\"/>."

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What this option actually does is configure which network protocol to prefer "
"when pushing source code for these modules. Normally the very-efficient "
"<literal>git</literal> protocol is used, but this may be blocked in some "
"networks (e.g. corporate intranets, public Wi-Fi). An alternative protocol "
"which is much better supported is the <literal>https</literal> protocol used "
"for Internet web sites."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are using one of these constrained networks you can set this option "
"to <userinput>http</userinput> to prefer <literal>https</literal> "
"communications instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may also need the <link linkend=\"conf-http-proxy\">http-proxy</link> "
"option if an HTTP proxy is also needed for network traffic."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In any other situation you should not set this option as the default "
"protocol is most efficient."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: conf-options-table.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "git-repository-base"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: conf-options-table.docbook:122 conf-options-table.docbook:1416
#, no-c-format
msgid "1.12.1"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option is used to create a short name to reference a specific Git "
"repository base URL in later <link linkend=\"module-sets\">module set</link> "
"declarations, which is useful for quickly declaring many Git modules to "
"build."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must specify two things (separated by a space): The name to assign to "
"the base URL, and the actual base URL itself. For example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: conf-options-table.docbook:133
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "global\n"
#| "    <option><link linkend=\"conf-git-repository-base\">git-repository-"
#| "base</link></option> <replaceable>kde-git</replaceable> <replaceable>kde:"
#| "</replaceable>\n"
#| "end global\n"
#| "\n"
#| "module <replaceable>qt</replaceable>\n"
#| "    # Options removed for brevity\n"
#| "end module\n"
#| "\n"
#| "module-set <replaceable>kde-support-libs</replaceable>\n"
#| "    <option><link linkend=\"conf-repository\">repository</link></option> "
#| "<replaceable>kde-git</replaceable>\n"
#| "    <option><link linkend=\"conf-use-modules\">use-modules</link></"
#| "option> <replaceable>automoc</replaceable> <replaceable>attica</"
#| "replaceable> <replaceable>akonadi</replaceable>\n"
#| "end module-set\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# Other modules as necessary...\n"
#| "module <replaceable>kdesupport</replaceable>\n"
#| "end module"
msgid ""
"global\n"
"    # other options\n"
"    # This is the common path to all anonymous Git server modules.\n"
"    git-repository-base <replaceable>kde-git</replaceable> <replaceable>kde:"
"</replaceable>\n"
"end global\n"
"\n"
"# Module declarations\n"
"\n"
"module-set\n"
"    # Now you can use the alias you defined earlier, but <emphasis>only</"
"emphasis> in a module-set.\n"
"    repository <replaceable>kde-git</replaceable>\n"
"    <link linkend=\"conf-use-modules\">use-modules</link> "
"<replaceable>module1.git</replaceable> <replaceable>module2.git</"
"replaceable>\n"
"end module-set"
msgstr ""
"global\n"
"    <option><link linkend=\"conf-git-repository-base\">git-repository-base</"
"link></option> <replaceable>kde-git</replaceable> <replaceable>kde:</"
"replaceable>\n"
"end global\n"
"\n"
"module <replaceable>qt</replaceable>\n"
"    # Opcións retiradas por brevidade\n"
"end module\n"
"\n"
"module-set <replaceable>kde-support-libs</replaceable>\n"
"    <option><link linkend=\"conf-repository\">repository</link></option> "
"<replaceable>kde-git</replaceable>\n"
"    <option><link linkend=\"conf-use-modules\">use-modules</link></option> "
"<replaceable>automoc</replaceable> <replaceable>attica</replaceable> "
"<replaceable>akonadi</replaceable>\n"
"end module-set\n"
"\n"
"# Outros módulos…\n"
"module <replaceable>kdesupport</replaceable>\n"
"end module"

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The module-set's <literal>use-modules</literal> option created two modules "
"internally, with &kdesrc-build; behaving as if it had read:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: conf-options-table.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"module module1\n"
"    repository kde:<replaceable>module1.git</replaceable>\n"
"end module\n"
"\n"
"module module2\n"
"    repository kde:<replaceable>module2.git</replaceable>\n"
"end module"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <literal>kde:</literal> &git; repository prefix used above is a shortcut "
"which will be setup by &kdesrc-build; automatically. See the TechBase <ulink "
"url=\"https://techbase.kde.org/Development/Git/Configuration#URL_Renaming"
"\">URL Renaming</ulink> article for more information. Note that unlike most "
"other options, this option can be specified multiple times in order to "
"create as many aliases as necessary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is not required to use this option to take advantage of module-set, this "
"option exists to make it easy to use the same repository across many "
"different module sets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: conf-options-table.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "install-environment-driver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: conf-options-table.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "17.08"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Install a shell script that can be sourced in a user's profile setup scripts "
"to easily establish needed environment variables to run the Plasma desktop "
"built by &kdesrc-build;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:167 conf-options-table.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "This driver will alter the following files:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:170 conf-options-table.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kde-env-master.sh</filename> (normally found at "
"<filename>~/.config/kde-env-master.sh</filename>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:171 conf-options-table.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kde-env-user.sh</filename> (normally found at "
"<filename>~/.config/kde-env-user.sh</filename>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <filename>kde-env-user.sh</filename> is optional. It is intended for "
"user customizations (see the <ulink url=\"https://userbase.kde.org/"
"KDE_System_Administration/Environment_Variables#Troubleshooting_and_Debugging"
"\">Troubleshooting and Debugging</ulink> section of the &kde; UserBase for "
"examples of customizable settings), but these settings can be set elsewhere "
"by the user in their existing profile setup scripts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can disable this feature by setting this option to <replaceable>false</"
"replaceable>, and ensuring that the <link linkend=\"conf-install-session-"
"driver\">install-session-driver</link> option is also disabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:184 conf-options-table.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdesrc-build; will not overwrite your existing files (if present) unless "
"you also pass the <option><link linkend=\"cmdline-delete-my-settings\">--"
"delete-my-settings</link></option> command-line option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Related command-line option: --install-environment-driver, --no-install-"
"environment-driver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: conf-options-table.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "install-session-driver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: conf-options-table.docbook:198 conf-options-table.docbook:746
#: conf-options-table.docbook:1022 conf-options-table.docbook:1089
#: conf-options-table.docbook:1161 conf-options-table.docbook:1239
#: conf-options-table.docbook:1384
#, no-c-format
msgid "1.16"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kdesrc-build; will try to install a driver for the graphical "
"login manager that allows you to login to your &kdesrc-build;-built &kde; "
"desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: conf-options-table.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "~/.xsession"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you maintain your own login driver then you can disable this feature by "
"setting this option to <replaceable>false</replaceable>. If enabled, this "
"feature also enables the <link linkend=\"conf-install-environment-driver"
"\">install-environment-driver</link> feature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Related command-line option: --install-session-driver, --no-install-session-"
"driver"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: conf-options-table.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "niceness"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: conf-options-table.docbook:227 conf-options-table.docbook:241
#: conf-options-table.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "Integer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: conf-options-table.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "<member>10</member>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set this option to a number between 20 and 0. The higher the number, the "
"lower a priority &kdesrc-build; will set for itself, i.e. the higher the "
"number, the \"nicer\" the program is."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Related command-line option: <xref linkend=\"cmdline-nice\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: conf-options-table.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "num-cores"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: conf-options-table.docbook:242 conf-options-table.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Depends on system"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: conf-options-table.docbook:243 conf-options-table.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "20.07"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option is defined by &kdesrc-build; (when using <command>kdesrc-build --"
"generate-config</command>), set to be the number of available CPUs (as "
"indicated by the external application <application>nproc</application>). If "
"&kdesrc-build; cannot detect the number of CPUs, this value is set to 4."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: conf-options-table.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <xref linkend=\"make-options-example\"/> for an example of this option's "
"usage."
